#! name: fit
#! does: a network that learns a straight line from measures.csv
#! try: use programs/fit.grm ; load programs/measures.csv ; put x = 10 ; ask y
# A network that learns: y = k x + c, with k and c weights. Load measures.csv (columns x and y): each row is seen
# once, and k and c keep what they have learned (they are in the memory at the next session).
#     use programs/fit.grm ; load programs/measures.csv ; put x = 10 ; ask y
learn k = 0
learn c = 0
input x
input y
output y
relate model: y = k * x + c ± 0.5
